{
  "configuration_id": "config_010",
  "reason": "We have only one completed experiment (config_001: RNA-only, PCA-2000, singleprofile → 48.5% acc). The most fundamental uncertainty is whether the image modality contributes any signal at all, which determines whether multimodal fusion is worth pursuing. config_010 (image_only, singleprofile, ResNet50) is the cleanest possible comparison: it matches config_001 in profile setting (singleprofile) and uses a standard, simple encoder (ResNet50 analogous to PCA), isolating the modality effect with no confounds from aggregation, fusion, or learned RNA encoders. If image performs comparably or better than RNA, it justifies investing subsequent experiments in multimodal fusion and more complex image encoders. If it performs much worse, we can focus budget on RNA-side improvements (better encoders, multiprofile). This single experiment maximally reduces uncertainty about the most important design axis (modality) before committing to more complex configurations."
}

